  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 200 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThursday-Sunday:\nThe prolonged heat wave persists Thursday through the weekend,\nwith the impacts of a multi-day heat wave compounding. This is\nwell captured by the NWS HeatRisk, showing widespread major to\nextreme heat-related impacts. The extreme category is\ncharacterized by long duration of extreme heat with minimal or\nno overnight relief. Highs are progged to remain in the upper\n90s to around 100, with lows in the upper 70s to around 80. With\ndewpoints remaining in the upper 60s to lower 70s, heat index\nvalues remain around 100 to 110. An Extreme Heat Warning is in\neffect Thursday afternoon through Sunday evening. Any groups\nsensitive to heat, including the elderly and infants should \ntake the proper precautions from the heat through the weekend. \nStay hydrated and cool.\n\nOtherwise, the jet stream primarily remains suppressed to the \nnorth of the area. A secondary shortwave slides north of the \narea on Thursday, with 10-20% PoPs glancing central MO once \nagain. However, confidence remains low on this potential, with \nmost areas remaining dry.\n\nNext Week:\nEnsemble guidance is coming into a bit better agreement that a\nfront gets into the area late Sunday into Monday. Depending on\nlocation and positioning of jet stream, this could support some\nrelief from the heat. Early indications suggest a wide array of\ntemperatures from south to north across the area. It is\nplausible to see middle to upper 90s south and upper 80s/lower\n90s north. Thus, perhaps a brief in the heat for portions of the\narea, but not all. The uncertainty can be captured by\ninterquartile spreads around 8 to 10 degrees for high\ntemperatures next week. Additional rain chances (10-30%) \naccompany this pattern change.",
